---
import BaseLayout from "@layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { SITE_TITLE } from "@consts";
---

<BaseLayout title={`About – ${SITE_TITLE}`} description="About Nourished Journeys — practical mindfulness for real life, no apps required.">
  <article class="prose mx-auto max-w-4xl">
    <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 2rem;">
      <img
        src="/chester-profile.jpg"
        alt="Chester Beard"
        style="width: 180px; height: 180px; object-fit: cover; border-radius: 50%; margin: 0 auto 1rem; display: block; box-shadow: 0 4px 20px rgba(22, 33, 62, 0.12);"
      />
      <h1 style="margin-bottom: 0.25rem;">About Nourished Journeys</h1>
      <p style="color: #9AA899; font-style: italic;">Practical mindfulness for real life. No apps required.</p>
    </div>

    <h2>Why This Exists</h2>
    <p>I started Nourished Journeys after years of working in conservation — long days outdoors with organizations like the Sierra Club and The Nature Conservancy — where I saw firsthand how time in nature resets the mind. But I also saw the flip side: desk-bound stretches where stress accumulated, focus fractured, and the simplest habits felt impossible to maintain.</p>
    <p>I tried the apps. I tried the expensive programs. What actually worked were the low-tech practices: ten minutes with a notebook, a breathing technique before a difficult conversation, a short walk without headphones. Nothing fancy. Nothing that required a subscription.</p>
    <p>Nourished Journeys exists to share those practices — grounded in research, tested in real life, and written for people who want to feel better without turning self-improvement into another project.</p>

    <h2>What You'll Find Here</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Journaling</strong> — Techniques to process thoughts, set intentions, and track personal growth. From brain dumps to gratitude journals, with templates you can start using today.</li>
      <li><strong>Meditation</strong> — Practical guides for focus, relaxation, and inner peace. Including specific techniques for brain fog, insomnia, and decision fatigue.</li>
      <li><strong>Breathwork</strong> — Breathing techniques from pranayama traditions and modern science. Box breathing, 4-7-8, physiological sighs, and more — with an interactive visualizer to practice along.</li>
      <li><strong>Yoga</strong> — Physical practices connecting body, mind, and spirit. Pose guides, breathing integration, and the history behind the practice.</li>
      <li><strong>Mindfulness</strong> — Present-moment awareness techniques for daily life. Attention training, nervous system regulation, and the difference between mindfulness and meditation.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How Content Is Created</h2>
    <p>Every article on this site goes through the same process:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Research first</strong> — Claims are grounded in published studies, clinical research, or established tradition. Sources are cited where they add value.</li>
      <li><strong>Tested in practice</strong> — Techniques are described by someone who has actually done them, not just read about them. If something doesn't work as described elsewhere, that's noted.</li>
      <li><strong>Updated regularly</strong> — Content is revisited and revised as new research emerges or reader feedback highlights gaps. Each article shows its last modified date.</li>
      <li><strong>Not medical advice</strong> — Nothing here is a substitute for professional medical or mental health support. If you're dealing with a clinical condition, please work with a qualified professional.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What Makes This Different</h2>
    <p>Most wellness content online is either too vague ("just breathe!") or too clinical (dense research papers with no practical steps). Nourished Journeys sits in the middle: specific enough to actually do something with, accessible enough to understand without a PhD.</p>
    <p>No apps. No subscriptions. No equipment. Just practices that work, explained clearly, with enough science to trust them.</p>

    <h2>Get In Touch</h2>
    <p>Questions, feedback, or a topic you'd like covered? Reach out at <a href="mailto:buzzUW2@gmail.com">buzzUW2@gmail.com</a> or visit the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</p>

    <p>To get new articles delivered to your inbox, <a href="#newsletter">subscribe to the newsletter</a>.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
